<iscomment>
	TEMPLATENAME: payerAuthReturn.isml

	Rendered inside the step-up iframe the moment the ACS finishes the 3DS challenge.

	Deliberately does no payment work. It exists so that the parent window gets a same-origin
	signal at the exact moment the challenge ends: while the challenge is up the iframe is on the
	issuer's domain and the parent can see nothing inside it. Returning straight to
	PayerAuthValidation would mean that signal only arrived after validation, order placement and
	the confirmation email had all run - far too late to raise a spinner.

	It posts the completion message to the parent FIRST, then forwards the ACS's POST body on to
	PayerAuthValidation. Fields are forwarded generically because the set an ACS echoes back varies.
</iscomment>
<iscontent type="text/html" charset="UTF-8" compact="true"/>
<div class="payerauth-return">
	<iscomment>
		target="_self" keeps the forward inside this iframe, so PayerAuthValidation's response
		renders here and its checkoutRedirect script can drive window.top as it always has.
	</iscomment>
	<form id="payerAuthForwardForm" name="payerAuthForwardForm" action="${pdict.action}" method="POST" target="_self">
		<isloop items="${pdict.forwardedParams}" var="forwardedParam">
			<input type="hidden" name="${forwardedParam.name}" value="${forwardedParam.value}"/>
		</isloop>
	</form>

	<input type="hidden" id="payerAuthCompleteMessageType" value="${pdict.completeMessageType}"/>

	<script src="${URLUtils.staticURL('/js/payerAuthReturn.js')}"></script>
</div>
